UNIT renamed_mii
KIND FUNCTIONAL
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
FIDELITY spec
ANCHOR Wii U Mii data as stored by Super Mario Maker in a maker object: 96 bytes, Mii ID at offset 0x8, name at 0x1A, checksum in the last two bytes (measured from Miis a real game stored, 2026-11)
SIG renamed_mii(original: bytes, name: text, id: u64) -> bytes
ENVELOPE original is any byte string; name is any well-formed text; id is 0 to 4294967295.
DEPENDS-ON mii_checksum
DESCRIPTION A copy of a Mii with another name and ID, and its checksum redone so a game accepts it.
BEHAVIOR
R1 When original is not exactly 96 bytes long, the answer is original unchanged.
R2 Otherwise the answer is 96 bytes: a copy of original with only the three fields of R3, R4 and R5 changed. original itself is never changed.
R3 Bytes 0x8 to 0xB hold id, least significant byte first. CITED
R4 Bytes 0x1A to 0x2D hold the name as 10 UTF-16 code units, each least significant byte first. A name longer than 10 code units keeps its first 10 (a character outside the Basic Multilingual Plane is two code units and may be cut in half); a shorter one is followed by zero units up to 10. CITED
R5 The last two bytes hold mii_checksum of the first 94 bytes of the answer, most significant byte first. CITED
PROVENANCE recorded by rdv from mii/mii.go
ORACLE value -> oracles/renamed_mii.json CANONICAL-SHA256 c5445d39172f94af85551e637eed5d4ae392e9bcdc435dc8807cd467eaa2866d
NOTE rules written; no independent rebuild has been graded yet.
